          "case": "iff-forward",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "Definition of Two-body phase-space and formal coefficient data: Assume Countable Choice [[def-countable-choice]] and use the energy-vector, metric, and unit conventions of [[def-qft-example-data]]. A rest-energy parameter $\\mathsf M\\geq0$ is measured in joules. Its positive shell is parameterized by $p=(E,\\mathbf p)$ with $E=\\sqrt{|\\mathbf p|^2+\\mathsf M^2}>0$; the shell measure is $d\\nu_{\\mathsf M}=d^3\\mathbf p/((2\\pi)^3\\,2E)$. The value $\\mathsf M=0$, $\\mathbf p=0$ is excluded. Let $\\mathsf M_1,\\mathsf M_2\\geq0$ and let $s>(\\mathsf M_1+\\mathsf M_2)^2$. Define $$k_*=\\frac{\\sqrt{[s-(\\mathsf M_1+\\mathsf M_2)^2][s-(\\mathsf M_1-\\mathsf M_2)^2]}}{2\\sqrt{s}}, \\qquad E_i^*=\\sqrt{k_*^2+\\mathsf M_i^2}.$$ Both factors under the square root are positive, so $k_*>0$. On the Euclidean  The forward iff axis adds no separately stated converse hypothesis here; the recorded claim is the displayed construction, identity, implication or scope qualification, not a characterization by a new necessary-and-sufficient condition."
        },
        {
          "case": "iff-reverse",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "Definition of Two-body phase-space and formal coefficient data: Assume Countable Choice [[def-countable-choice]] and use the energy-vector, metric, and unit conventions of [[def-qft-example-data]]. A rest-energy parameter $\\mathsf M\\geq0$ is measured in joules. Its positive shell is parameterized by $p=(E,\\mathbf p)$ with $E=\\sqrt{|\\mathbf p|^2+\\mathsf M^2}>0$; the shell measure is $d\\nu_{\\mathsf M}=d^3\\mathbf p/((2\\pi)^3\\,2E)$. The value $\\mathsf M=0$, $\\mathbf p=0$ is excluded. Let $\\mathsf M_1,\\mathsf M_2\\geq0$ and let $s>(\\mathsf M_1+\\mathsf M_2)^2$. Define $$k_*=\\frac{\\sqrt{[s-(\\mathsf M_1+\\mathsf M_2)^2][s-(\\mathsf M_1-\\mathsf M_2)^2]}}{2\\sqrt{s}}, \\qquad E_i^*=\\sqrt{k_*^2+\\mathsf M_i^2}.$$ Both factors under the square root are positive, so $k_*>0$. On the Euclidean  The reverse iff axis adds no separately stated converse hypothesis here; the recorded claim is the displayed construction, identity, implication or scope qualification, not a characterization by a new necessary-and-sufficient condition."
