      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-46",
        "notes": "Read all four steps against finite Pauli/Dirac block products and SI conventions. Smooth A preserves C_c^infinity; direct commutator has +iq hbar epsilon B, contraction i epsilon/2 gives -q hbar Sigma dot B, and beta mixed terms cancel. m>0 makes the polynomial first-degree coefficient unique. g_s=2 is equality of formal charge coefficients, so q=0 is a specialization rather than division by zero. No closure, spectrum, square-root theorem, radiative or empirical assertion follows. Reader/refuter no findings."
