          "reason": "Example of Formal Dirac spin coefficient in a uniform field: The two spin eigenvalues give opposite energy coefficients in the same uniform field. Their gap matches the cyclotron angular-frequency coefficient for charge magnitude $e$ and mass $m$. The specified witness, fixed coordinate space or supplied Hilbert/test objects are the inputs of this assertion; it does not assert a separate existence result after replacing them by an empty underlying set."
        },
